# [[.Title]]

A Steward plugin for [[.Title]], built with [`@steward/plugin`](https://github.com/treno-dev/steward/tree/main/sdk/plugin/js).

## Run

```sh
npm install
npm start
```

Node runs `src/plugin.ts` directly. Steward starts the plugin itself and talks to it over gRPC.
Running it by hand prints the handshake line the runner reads, and nothing else on standard output.
Write logs to stderr.

Run `npm run check` to type-check.

## Where things are

`src/plugin.ts` declares the integration (what it needs to connect), each kind of resource and the
handlers Steward calls: `provision`, `deprovision`, `grantAccess`, `revokeAccess` and `getAccess`.
Each handler is annotated with the request and response types the SDK exports. Delete the handlers
you do not need: Steward offers only what you implement.

To add a kind of resource, call `plugin.resource({ kind, ... })` again with its own inputs, outputs and
handlers.

See the [SDK README](https://github.com/treno-dev/steward/blob/main/sdk/plugin/js/README.md) for
everything a plugin can declare.
